  # O ANG word-initially carries a vowel-initial syllable and
  # romanizes as the ayn (Note 6: "ອ is used in initial position for
  # syllables beginning with a vowel, thus: ອີກ (ʻīk)"); this runs
  # before the consonant+vowel pair rows so the vowel-syllable carriers
  # ອັ ອາ ອິ ອີ ... render ʻ plus the vowel. Elsewhere ອ is the vowel
  # ǭ (default row below).
  parallel {
    sub { from "ອ" to "ʻ" before boundary }
  }

